{"config":{"frameFollowsTheme":true,"frameMinHeight":"320px","frameWidth":"880px","label":{"$i18n":"canvas.label"}},"id":"canvas","slots":{"frame":[{"config":{"direction":"vertical","gap":12,"padding":24},"id":"mock","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"mock.payment.title"},"variant":"title"},"id":"mock-title","type":"Text"},{"config":{"label":{"$i18n":"mock.payment.submit"},"variant":"primary"},"id":"mock-submit","type":"Button"}]},"type":"Stack"}],"palette":[{"config":{"appearance":"palette","label":{"$i18n":"tool.label"}},"id":"tool-palette","slots":{"content":[{"config":{"appearance":"palette","icon":"mouse-pointer-2","kbd":"V","label":{"$i18n":"tool.select"},"responsive":{"compact":{"iconOnly":true}},"selected":true},"id":"tool-select","type":"Segment"},{"config":{"activeTone":"annotation","appearance":"palette","icon":"message-circle-plus","kbd":"C","label":{"$i18n":"tool.comment"},"responsive":{"compact":{"iconOnly":true}}},"id":"tool-comment","type":"Segment"},{"config":{"appearance":"palette","icon":"hand","kbd":"I","label":{"$i18n":"tool.interact"},"responsive":{"compact":{"iconOnly":true}}},"id":"tool-interact","type":"Segment"}]},"type":"SegmentedControl"}]},"type":"CanvasStage"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Canvas: Preview failure","spec":{"accessibility":["Title and body are one alert region keyed on the failing generation, so a repeated failure is announced again; the icon is decorative.","Retry Preview stays focusable while it is pending and says so with aria-disabled and a status text, never color alone.","Reason, detail and identities are marked not to be translated."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (ContextBar, ContextChip, Badge, Button, Alert, Disclosure, Stack, Text, CanvasStage, SegmentedControl, Segment); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","The failure strip is an Alert Widget: the real strip is a hairline-separated band with an octagon icon and no card border, and its details are a definition list.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities (the reason code, the detail and the session and generation identifiers); en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["The Workbench canvas has a View open and a Preview session that is live. A generation failed in a way that cannot recover by itself; the diagnostic stays until the Preview recovers, the render context is replaced or the session ends.","The base state is a lost connection (transport) with the details collapsed; Variants show each recognized reason, a reason the Workbench has no copy for, the expanded details, and Retry Preview while a fresh preview starts and when it has not answered.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme; the bar above and the canvas below are the Workbench chrome of the View page."],"intent":"Show the inline diagnostic under the canvas bar when the Preview session continues but the Preview can no longer be driven (a non-recoverable failure of the connection, the runtime, the protocol or the capabilities), with its one shared recovery action and the technical details one click away.","interactionRules":["The title names the failure category and the body says what is unavailable and what can be done, from the reason when the Workbench recognizes it, else from the category; the raw reason, the detail and the Preview session and runtime generation identities appear only under Technical details.","Retry Preview is the one recovery action for every failure and every reason; while the fresh preview it started is still in its handshake it shows a spinner and is not pressed again, and after five seconds without an answer it is offered again with a note.","The diagnostic is announced as an alert; when the Preview recovers while focus is inside it, focus moves to the canvas.","The canvas keeps its frame, zoom and tools, but highlighting and selecting a Widget are unavailable until a fresh preview answers."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"}],"requirements":["01a11687-375e-7667-b8f1-59389fdd9780","01a11687-3828-7160-b15b-13827988070e","01a11687-386c-764f-98fd-cf19dc3d0013","01a11658-18a0-7b94-8411-17b46d344429"]},"variants":{"capability-missing-feature":{"requirements":["01a11687-37a0-77bb-a857-5f7804b7c306"],"state":{"f-capability-missing-feature":{"visible":true},"f-capability-unsupported-version":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-capability-conflict":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-identity-reuse":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-invalid-message":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-invalid-state":{"visible":false},"f-runtime-unavailable":{"visible":false},"f-transport-channel":{"visible":false},"f-unrecognized-reason":{"visible":false}}},"capability-unsupported-version":{"requirements":["01a11687-37a0-77bb-a857-5f7804b7c306"],"state":{"f-capability-missing-feature":{"visible":false},"f-capability-unsupported-version":{"visible":true},"f-protocol-capability-conflict":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-identity-reuse":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-invalid-message":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-invalid-state":{"visible":false},"f-runtime-unavailable":{"visible":false},"f-transport-channel":{"visible":false},"f-unrecognized-reason":{"visible":false}}},"details-open":{"state":{"f-transport-channel-details":{"open":true}}},"protocol-capability-conflict":{"requirements":["01a11687-37a0-77bb-a857-5f7804b7c306"],"state":{"f-capability-missing-feature":{"visible":false},"f-capability-unsupported-version":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-capability-conflict":{"visible":true},"f-protocol-identity-reuse":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-invalid-message":{"visible":false},"f-protocol-invalid-state":{"visible":false},"f-runtime-unavailable":{"vis